.SH GETTING STARTED
.SS Real\-Time Setup
.sp
Before starting using scmlpick in real\-time you have to be sure in complete the following steps:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Create profile in the pipelines section in the module configuration (see \fI\%pipelines.profiles\fP\&.)
.IP 2. 3
Create and configure pick target and location target groups in the profile. (see \fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.pickTargetGroup\fP and \fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.locTargetGroup\fP)
.IP 3. 3
Create a \fBbinding profile\fP with pick enable option (see \fI\%Bindings\fP), the name should match with the module profile created in step 1.
.IP 4. 3
Assign the binding profile to stations/streams in \fI\%scconfig\fP (or edit bindings files).
.IP 5. 3
Start your messaging: \fBscmaster start\fP (or your standard SeisComP workflow).
.IP 6. 3
Launch \fBscmlpick\fP:
.INDENT 3.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
scmlpick \-u user \-\-debug
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For executing on the command line simply call it with appropriate options, e.g:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
seiscomp exec scmlpick \-h
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Next Steps
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Create \fBmodule profiles\fP (see \fI\%Module Profiles\fP) to separate dataflows and create specific processing for specific purposes.
.IP \(bu 2
Depending the number of stations and resources available configure ray parameters (see permormance)
.IP \(bu 2
Tune critial parameters like P and S models, probability thresholds, time windows lenght overlaps and more in the module configuration.
.IP \(bu 2
Use (see \fI\%Playback\fP) to postprocessing or validate parameters runing in playback mode with mseed files or historical data.
.UNINDENT
.SH MODULE PROFILES
.sp
In \fBscmlpick\fP, in contrast to other SeisComP modules, creating aliases is \fBnot\fP recommended.
Each alias starts a separate instance that runs in parallel and increases CPU/RAM usage.
Instead, run a single instance that processes all stations and use (see \fI\%pipelines.profiles\fP)
to define different workflows. Profiles let you run multiple independent pipelines
within one process, avoiding the need for \fBscmlpick\fP aliases.
.sp
Each profile can define its own:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.pickTargetGroup\fP all picks emitted by this profile are published to that specific messaging group.
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.locTargetGroup\fP this profile subscribes to locations from that messaging group.
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.authorTarget\fP locations carrying this author are checked against the profile’s quality\-control parameters.
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%pipelines.profiles.$name.region\fP polygon used to evaluate (filter/validate) locations processed by this profile.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Segment of scmlpick.cfg incuding two profiles:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# List with profiles names.
pipelines.profiles = PROF1, PROF2

# This is the name of the group to send pick messages for specific profile
pipelines.profiles.PROF1.pickTargetGroup = PPROF1

# This is the name of the group to send location messages for specific profile
pipelines.profiles.PROF1.locTargetGroup = LPROF1

# This author should match the origin (location) author for locations to be
# checked against quality control parameters.
pipelines.profiles.PROF1.authorTarget = LOCSATPROF1

# The BNA file defining regions (closed polygons) or tuple with 4 elements.
# Inside this region, the origin evaluation status is TrueOrgEvalStat, and
# outside is FalseOrgEvalStat. If this is set to none, then the origin location
# will not be checked against any polygon.
pipelines.profiles.PROF1.region = @DATADIR@/scmlpick/bna/PROF1.bna

# This is the name of the group to send pick messages for specific profile
pipelines.profiles.PROF2.pickTargetGroup = PPROF2

# This is the name of the group to send location messages for specific profile
pipelines.profiles.PROF2.locTargetGroup = LPROF2

# This author should match the origin (location) author for locations to be
# checked against quality control parameters.
pipelines.profiles.PROF2.authorTarget = LOCSATPROF2

# The BNA file defining regions (closed polygons) or tuple with 4 elements.
# Inside this region, the origin evaluation status is TrueOrgEvalStat, and
# outside is FalseOrgEvalStat. If this is set to none, then the origin location
# will not be checked against any polygon.
pipelines.profiles.PROF2.region = @DATADIR@/scmlpick/bna/PROF2.bna
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Each \fBmodule profile\fP must have a corresponding \fBbinding profile\fP that
associates the profile with specific stations; see \fI\%Bindings\fP\&.
The \fBmodule profile name must match the binding profile name\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH BINDINGS
.sp
In SeisComP, \fIbindings\fP attach module\-specific parameters to stations. \fBscmlpick\fP
uses bindings to activate specific stations to be processed by an \fBscmlpick\fP profile.
.SS Where to Configure
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
In \fI\%scconfig\fP assign the binding to the desired stations (bindings tab).
.IP \(bu 2
Or edit files under \fB$SEISCOMP_ROOT/etc/bindings/scmlpick/\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
Each binding enables picking for the stations \fBbound\fP to it:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%profiles.$name.pickEnable\fP Boolean flag to enable picking in this binding.
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can also set a station\-specific \fBfilter\fP\&. This filter is applied at the
beginning of the processing chain, before the ML algorithm runs:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%profiles.$name.filter\fP Parameter following the standard SeisComP filter grammar (\fI\%reference\fP).
.UNINDENT
.SH PLAYBACK
.sp
\fBscmlpick\fP supports \fBplayback\fP for offline (non–real\-time) processing. This mode is
useful for validation, benchmarking, parameter tuning, and research.
.SS Data sources
.sp
Playback can run against:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPre\-downloaded miniSEED files\fP fastest and fully repeatable.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHistorical data via the configured SeisComP RecordStream\fP (e.g., FDSN/CAPS/SeedLink).
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Querying large time windows from a RecordStream can be slow and will re\-fetch data
on every run. Prefer RecordStream playback for \fBshort\fP time intervals or \fBone\-off\fP
executions. For repeated experiments, use local miniSEED files.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Requirements
.sp
Playback uses the \fBsame configuration\fP as real\-time mode:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A \fBmodule profile\fP (see \fI\%Module Profiles\fP).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBindings\fP whose profile name \fBmatches\fP the module profile (see \fI\%Bindings\fP).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStations\fP assigned to that binding profile.
.IP \(bu 2
A valid data source: miniSEED files available locally \fBor\fP a correctly configured
RecordStream endpoint.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Keep \fI\%eqcct.windowLength\fP/\fI\%eqcct.timeShift\fP and other configuration parameters (see Tuning)
consistent with your real\-time setup if you want comparable latency and behavior between modes.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Command\-line options
.sp
Use the following options to run \fBscmlpick\fP in \fBplayback\fP mode.
.SS Input source (choose one)
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-recordstream\fP
Read historical data directly from a SeisComP RecordStream (e.g., FDSN/CAPS/SeedLink).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-mseed\-files <PATH>\fP
Read from one or more local miniSEED files, or a directory containing them.
.UNINDENT
.SS Playback window & profile
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-profile <NAME>\fP
Select the module profile to use. The profile name must match an existing
module profile \fBand\fP its corresponding binding profile.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-start \(dqYYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM:SS\(dq\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-end   \(dqYYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM:SS\(dq\fP
Time window for playback, applied to the chosen input source.
.UNINDENT
.SS Output
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-output\-file <FILE>\fP
Write results to an XML file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-database\fP
Send results directly to the SeisComP database.
.UNINDENT
.SS Ray parallelism (optional)
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-cpu\-number <N>\fP
Number of CPUs available to Ray. If omitted, the value from the module configuration is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-max\-tasks <N>\fP
Maximum number of concurrent tasks sent to the predictor. If omitted, the configured
default is used.
.UNINDENT
.SS Running Playback
.sp
\fIUsing local miniSEED:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
scmlpick \e
  \-\-playback \e
  \-\-profile playback \e
  \-\-mseed\-files /data/mseed/2025\-08\-01/ \e
  \-\-start \(dq2025\-08\-01 00:00:00\(dq \e
  \-\-end   \(dq2025\-08\-01 06:00:00\(dq \e
  \-\-output\-file /tmp/scmlpick_playback.xml \e
  \-u user \e
  \-\-debug
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fIUsing RecordStream:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
scmlpick \e
  \-\-playback \e
  \-\-profile playback \e
  \-\-recordstream \e
  \-\-start \(dq2025\-08\-01 00:00:00\(dq \e
  \-\-end   \(dq2025\-08\-01 03:00:00\(dq \e
  \-\-database
  \-u user \e
  \-\-debug
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH TUNING
.sp
Controls which pre\-trained models are used and how strict the decision rules are.
Select P/S models appropriate for your seismicity and set probability thresholds
that govern when picks are emitted; overlap and batch size affect latency and throughput.
